    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n54055" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταίθω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>burn down, burn to ashes</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταίθουσα . . δαλόν</span> (Canter for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ᾽ αἴθουσα</span>) <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				607
			</span></i>(lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σὺ δ᾽ οὖν κάταιθε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Andr.</u>
					258
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕφαπτε καὶ κάταιθε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Th.</u>
					730
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρὶ καταίθεται τέραμνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					1296
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			metaph., <i>kindle, rouse</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				249
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔρως με καταίθει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					7.56
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταίθεσθαι ἐπί τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					2.40
				</span></i>
			:—<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				359
			</span></i> is corrupt.</div>
